1
00:03:01,981 --> 00:03:31,961
We'll be right back.

2
00:03:31,981 --> 00:04:01,961
We'll be right back.

3
00:04:01,981 --> 00:04:31,961
We'll be right back.

4
00:04:31,981 --> 00:05:01,961
We'll be right back.

5
00:05:01,961 --> 00:05:03,961
We'll be right back.

6
00:05:03,961 --> 00:05:06,681
Hey, stop jumping around!

7
00:05:06,941 --> 00:05:07,901
We're getting nowhere!

8
00:05:08,941 --> 00:05:12,361
I was hoping my four powers would be enough, but I guess not.

9
00:05:12,561 --> 00:05:18,521
I'm afraid I haven't mastered the finger pistols yet, but I've got a little stand-in that should do the job quite nicely.

10
00:05:18,521 --> 00:05:21,461
All right, this is my chance to go to the next car!

11
00:05:21,461 --> 00:05:23,521
Hey, I thought we were having a fight here!

12
00:05:24,101 --> 00:05:25,221
He thinks he's smart.

13
00:05:28,701 --> 00:05:30,141
I got you now.

14
00:05:30,141 --> 00:05:41,021
Nice try, but I saw that coming from a mile away!

15
00:05:41,021 --> 00:05:55,581
You son of a bitch!

16
00:05:55,581 --> 00:05:57,041
Ouchie finger!

17
00:05:57,041 --> 00:06:00,361
This ain't good.

18
00:06:00,801 --> 00:06:02,241
It's got my number now.

19
00:06:04,241 --> 00:06:04,801
Take this!

20
00:06:04,801 --> 00:06:07,801
Just grazed me!

21
00:06:07,801 --> 00:06:10,281
Sure moves around a lot, though.

22
00:06:10,281 --> 00:06:13,881
I know your weak point.

23
00:06:15,001 --> 00:06:17,261
It's your back, isn't it?

24
00:06:17,501 --> 00:06:21,601
And that's not counting your brain, which is an obvious weakness, too.

25
00:06:21,961 --> 00:06:24,721
At this rate, it's only a matter of time before you're finished.

26
00:06:24,721 --> 00:06:27,041
Don't get ahead of yourself, pal.

27
00:06:27,601 --> 00:06:30,661
I got a move that'll get rid of my weak point easy.

28
00:06:31,081 --> 00:06:31,601
Frankie!

29
00:06:32,661 --> 00:06:33,341
Invincible!

30
00:06:34,181 --> 00:06:34,981
Eat that!

31
00:06:38,321 --> 00:06:40,581
Now do you give up, weasel face?

32
00:06:41,801 --> 00:06:42,321
Yes.

33
00:06:43,741 --> 00:06:46,241
That's so stupid, I don't even have a comeback.

34
00:06:46,241 --> 00:06:54,761
What's going on?

35
00:06:55,701 --> 00:06:57,741
How did you get here in the first place?

36
00:06:57,921 --> 00:06:59,121
This is dangerous, you know.

37
00:07:01,341 --> 00:07:05,141
Ma'am, I can hardly answer if you bombard me with questions like that.

38
00:07:05,421 --> 00:07:07,521
Let's just calm down and take it slowly.

39
00:07:08,721 --> 00:07:10,741
Ah, shall I pour you some coffee, perhaps?

40
00:07:11,001 --> 00:07:12,361
Stop fooling around!

41
00:07:16,241 --> 00:07:17,921
What are you...

42
00:07:17,921 --> 00:07:18,821
Pleased to meet you.

43
00:07:19,021 --> 00:07:21,541
I'm Sniper King, the King of the Snipers.

44
00:07:21,761 --> 00:07:25,241
To make a long story short, I've come to rescue you.

45
00:07:26,541 --> 00:07:27,901
You're really serious.

46
00:07:28,401 --> 00:07:29,661
I'm not alone, of course.

47
00:07:30,561 --> 00:07:33,081
Your friend Sanji and a cyborg thug named Frankie

48
00:07:33,081 --> 00:07:35,641
are currently engaged in battle on this train.

49
00:07:36,101 --> 00:07:38,761
They kept the enemy busy long enough for me to come here.

50
00:07:39,461 --> 00:07:42,201
Furthermore, Captain Luffy and the rest of the Straw Hats

51
00:07:42,201 --> 00:07:44,241
are following closely on another sea train.

52
00:07:44,241 --> 00:07:47,141
I hear he's bringing a small army with him.

53
00:07:54,201 --> 00:07:57,761
On my way here, I peeked inside the other train cars.

54
00:07:58,321 --> 00:08:01,041
Frankly, I believe the four agents in the car behind us

55
00:08:01,041 --> 00:08:02,521
may prove too great a challenge.

56
00:08:03,341 --> 00:08:06,001
If possible, I would like to escape with you

57
00:08:06,001 --> 00:08:07,501
before Sanji has to face them.

58
00:08:07,501 --> 00:08:16,081
Come, let's run away.

59
00:08:16,601 --> 00:08:16,901
Together!

60
00:08:16,901 --> 00:08:25,401
What's the matter?

61
00:08:25,801 --> 00:08:26,921
There's no need to worry.

62
00:08:27,261 --> 00:08:29,061
I've made all of the necessary preparations.

63
00:08:30,661 --> 00:08:31,081
Here.

64
00:08:31,421 --> 00:08:32,861
These octo-shoes are for you.

65
00:08:33,381 --> 00:08:35,001
If you use them on your hands and feet,

66
00:08:35,201 --> 00:08:36,281
you can climb through the window

67
00:08:36,281 --> 00:08:38,261
and stick to the outer panels of the sea train.

68
00:08:38,741 --> 00:08:40,701
Quickly, put them on before they notice.

69
00:08:40,701 --> 00:08:41,781
I won't go.

70
00:08:42,161 --> 00:08:42,741
Why not?

71
00:08:43,801 --> 00:08:46,101
I don't know why you're doing this.

72
00:08:46,941 --> 00:08:50,201
I told you very clearly that I wouldn't see you again.

73
00:08:50,561 --> 00:08:52,921
I said that I would never return to the Straw Hats.

74
00:08:58,601 --> 00:09:00,401
The situation has changed.

75
00:09:00,901 --> 00:09:02,601
They know why you turned yourself in.

76
00:09:02,601 --> 00:09:06,401
That ice gentleman from the shipyard clarified everything.

77
00:09:08,241 --> 00:09:10,301
So he survived after all?

78
00:09:11,221 --> 00:09:13,941
But still, that doesn't change my mind.

79
00:09:14,801 --> 00:09:16,821
I won't go with you no matter what.

80
00:09:17,241 --> 00:09:18,461
Enough with that already.

81
00:09:19,221 --> 00:09:20,261
Don't you get it?

82
00:09:20,501 --> 00:09:23,141
They aren't so weak that they need you to worry about them.

83
00:09:24,061 --> 00:09:25,461
What were you thinking?

84
00:09:25,841 --> 00:09:27,461
Accepting such a stupid deal

85
00:09:27,461 --> 00:09:29,141
before talking to the rest of the crew.

86
00:09:30,481 --> 00:09:32,461
You think they'd be happy to go on?

87
00:09:32,841 --> 00:09:34,081
Knowing that one of their friends

88
00:09:34,081 --> 00:09:35,661
had thrown her life away for them?

89
00:09:36,141 --> 00:09:37,781
Now that they know why you left,

90
00:09:38,001 --> 00:09:40,401
they'll follow you to the depths of hell if they have to.

91
00:09:40,661 --> 00:09:43,281
And they'll bust every skull they can on the way there.

92
00:09:44,261 --> 00:09:45,661
You don't get it, do you?

93
00:09:46,041 --> 00:09:48,321
That's the kind of guy Luffy is.

94
00:09:49,201 --> 00:09:51,561
How many times do I have to tell you this?

95
00:09:51,881 --> 00:09:53,621
Even if you think you can save me,

96
00:09:53,681 --> 00:09:54,901
I don't want your help.

97
00:09:55,141 --> 00:09:56,781
Don't you care how I feel?

98
00:09:58,421 --> 00:10:00,021
Come on, give me a break.

99
00:10:02,601 --> 00:10:05,041
Hey, keep it down in there, you.

100
00:10:07,661 --> 00:10:08,681
What's the matter?

101
00:10:09,361 --> 00:10:11,461
Now that we're getting close to Eni's lobby,

102
00:10:11,881 --> 00:10:13,721
is that cool exterior of yours

103
00:10:13,721 --> 00:10:15,381
finally starting to melt away?

104
00:10:16,121 --> 00:10:17,941
Well, you can cry all you like,

105
00:10:18,201 --> 00:10:20,301
but there's no point in lamenting your fate

106
00:10:20,301 --> 00:10:22,121
after it's already been sealed.

107
00:10:22,661 --> 00:10:23,841
Really, I'm fine.

108
00:10:23,841 --> 00:10:26,841
Strange.

109
00:10:28,041 --> 00:10:30,161
That's not the reaction I was expecting.

110
00:10:31,221 --> 00:10:33,121
I can't put my finger on it,

111
00:10:33,381 --> 00:10:35,321
but there's something different about her.

112
00:10:36,921 --> 00:10:38,961
Maybe it's just my imagination?

113
00:10:40,961 --> 00:10:42,441
I said I'm fine.

114
00:10:43,401 --> 00:10:45,401
Now please, just leave me alone.

115
00:10:45,401 --> 00:10:48,241
This is definitely fishy.

116
00:10:48,801 --> 00:10:51,261
Why is she goofing off at a time like this?

117
00:10:56,261 --> 00:10:56,821
Rabbit ears?

118
00:10:58,121 --> 00:11:00,341
Kai, would you take this seriously?

119
00:11:00,761 --> 00:11:02,481
You can't just quit because you are losing.

120
00:11:02,921 --> 00:11:04,041
Get up and fight me.

121
00:11:04,241 --> 00:11:05,221
I'll spit on you.

122
00:11:06,101 --> 00:11:09,121
I'd watch my weasel mouth if I were you, punk.

123
00:11:09,741 --> 00:11:10,921
I'm not quitting.

124
00:11:11,101 --> 00:11:12,481
I'm just getting started.

125
00:11:13,841 --> 00:11:16,321
Anyway, this is nothing but bad luck.

126
00:11:17,461 --> 00:11:19,281
Well, bad luck for you, I mean.

127
00:11:19,541 --> 00:11:20,781
I'm doing great.

128
00:11:24,421 --> 00:11:27,441
Did I mention I was super this week?

129
00:11:29,001 --> 00:11:31,521
It's not a good time to make me angry.

130
00:11:35,221 --> 00:11:36,921
Let me ask you something, brother.

131
00:11:37,521 --> 00:11:40,861
Have you ever heard of a creature they call a centaur?

132
00:11:41,101 --> 00:11:41,441
Huh?

133
00:11:42,101 --> 00:11:44,721
You mean those things that are human from the waist up

134
00:11:44,721 --> 00:11:46,401
and like a horse from the waist down?

135
00:11:46,821 --> 00:11:48,281
Yeah, what about them?

136
00:11:51,361 --> 00:11:53,281
Convert!

137
00:12:05,221 --> 00:12:09,901
No way.

138
00:12:10,261 --> 00:12:11,101
That's ridiculous.

139
00:12:17,101 --> 00:12:17,181
Frankie!

140
00:12:19,561 --> 00:12:20,601
Centaur Mo!

141
00:12:20,821 --> 00:12:21,521
It's backwards!

142
00:12:21,861 --> 00:12:24,221
Your head's supposed to be in the front, not your crotch!

143
00:12:24,221 --> 00:12:33,101
You call this backwards?

144
00:12:33,741 --> 00:12:36,841
Just wait till I rearrange your face, weasel boy.

145
00:12:36,841 --> 00:12:57,101
Are we there yet?

146
00:12:57,261 --> 00:12:58,421
Where's Bash and Tom?

147
00:12:58,481 --> 00:12:59,661
It's huffing Tom!

148
00:12:59,781 --> 00:13:01,961
Anyway, get inside before you catch a cold.

149
00:13:02,141 --> 00:13:04,601
You just changed clothes and you're soaking wet already.

150
00:13:04,601 --> 00:13:07,761
I don't care, it's more awesome up here!

151
00:13:08,621 --> 00:13:09,261
Fine.

152
00:13:10,761 --> 00:13:12,361
Now, gum gum!

153
00:13:12,921 --> 00:13:15,441
300 caliber cannon!

154
00:13:16,081 --> 00:13:16,401
Boom!

155
00:13:17,121 --> 00:13:17,361
Whoa!

156
00:13:18,401 --> 00:13:18,761
Yeah!

157
00:13:19,021 --> 00:13:20,061
We got a family!

158
00:13:20,801 --> 00:13:22,901
Would all of you stop screwing around?

159
00:13:24,341 --> 00:13:25,621
We're bored.

160
00:13:25,981 --> 00:13:27,661
Then polish your weapons or something.

161
00:13:27,861 --> 00:13:28,921
What's wrong with you?

162
00:13:28,921 --> 00:13:36,341
Yeah, I tried to tell those guys the same thing earlier, but they wouldn't listen to me.

163
00:13:40,621 --> 00:13:42,241
Hey, check it out!

164
00:13:42,941 --> 00:13:45,301
There's a train in front of us!

165
00:13:48,021 --> 00:13:49,861
It's the puffing Tom!

166
00:13:49,861 --> 00:13:55,421
Seems a bit early, don't you think?

167
00:13:56,161 --> 00:13:57,721
Who's in my armpit?

168
00:13:59,721 --> 00:14:01,021
I can't move!

169
00:14:04,141 --> 00:14:04,821
Damn it.

170
00:14:05,021 --> 00:14:06,521
What's going to happen to us now?

171
00:14:06,761 --> 00:14:08,281
There's no engine on this car.

172
00:14:08,701 --> 00:14:10,241
All we can do is wait it out.

173
00:14:11,301 --> 00:14:12,361
Another way!

174
00:14:12,361 --> 00:14:15,081
Oh, this storm is still pretty bad.

175
00:14:15,261 --> 00:14:16,841
You think someone will come save us?

176
00:14:17,161 --> 00:14:18,941
We're in big trouble if they don't.

177
00:14:19,581 --> 00:14:20,201
Hey, guys!

178
00:14:20,421 --> 00:14:22,041
There's something approaching from behind!

179
00:14:22,301 --> 00:14:22,661
Really?

180
00:14:23,001 --> 00:14:24,401
It must be a rescue ship.

181
00:14:24,701 --> 00:14:26,021
I don't think so.

182
00:14:26,461 --> 00:14:28,661
Actually, it looks like it's coming on the railway.

183
00:14:29,121 --> 00:14:30,001
There's no way.

184
00:14:30,601 --> 00:14:33,801
There's only one sea train in the world and we're on it right now.

185
00:14:33,901 --> 00:14:35,321
Besides, it's Aqua Laguna.

186
00:14:35,321 --> 00:14:37,801
No one could make it out of Water 7 in this weather.

187
00:14:37,861 --> 00:14:40,321
Well, if it's not a train, then...

188
00:14:43,141 --> 00:14:46,081
What the heck is it?

189
00:14:47,281 --> 00:14:49,041
That's the puffing Tom, all right.

190
00:14:49,301 --> 00:14:50,601
But it's just a caboose.

191
00:14:50,821 --> 00:14:51,821
There's no engine.

192
00:14:52,521 --> 00:14:54,181
And it doesn't look like it's moving.

193
00:14:54,341 --> 00:14:55,341
That can't be right.

194
00:14:55,441 --> 00:14:56,781
What's going on here?

195
00:14:57,221 --> 00:14:58,941
Does this mean it got detached somehow?

196
00:15:00,241 --> 00:15:03,301
Maybe something happened and Sanji and Usopp are on there.

197
00:15:03,301 --> 00:15:05,061
Big bro Frankie, too.

198
00:15:06,041 --> 00:15:08,721
Well, I hope not, because we're about to crash into them.

199
00:15:09,021 --> 00:15:10,461
Frankie, hit the brake!

200
00:15:10,841 --> 00:15:12,781
I already told you now, didn't I?

201
00:15:12,861 --> 00:15:13,881
We don't got one.

202
00:15:15,321 --> 00:15:16,501
We're going to crash!

203
00:15:18,721 --> 00:15:21,001
Luffy, what are you going to do?

204
00:15:21,501 --> 00:15:23,581
I'm flying over to see what's up.

205
00:15:23,721 --> 00:15:24,821
Now come, go!

206
00:15:25,281 --> 00:15:26,081
Rockets!

207
00:15:27,461 --> 00:15:28,001
Whoa!

208
00:15:29,521 --> 00:15:31,161
There's something in the sky!

209
00:15:31,161 --> 00:15:39,121
What happened?

210
00:15:47,881 --> 00:15:49,081
Ow, ow, ow!

211
00:15:49,421 --> 00:15:50,241
All right!

212
00:15:50,641 --> 00:15:51,501
I made it!

213
00:15:52,501 --> 00:15:54,401
Who the hell is this weirdo?

214
00:15:54,561 --> 00:15:55,141
Hello?

215
00:15:55,141 --> 00:15:57,441
Saji, are you in here?

216
00:15:59,641 --> 00:16:00,761
Poor Usopp.

217
00:16:02,021 --> 00:16:03,101
Hey, Saji!

218
00:16:04,181 --> 00:16:05,181
You hear me?

219
00:16:06,301 --> 00:16:07,301
Maybe over there.

220
00:16:07,301 --> 00:16:15,921
Wait a sec, I know that face!

221
00:16:16,601 --> 00:16:18,221
It's Straw Hat Luffy!

222
00:16:18,221 --> 00:16:25,981
Hello?

223
00:16:25,981 --> 00:16:29,141
Are you there?

224
00:16:29,561 --> 00:16:30,101
Saji!

225
00:16:30,941 --> 00:16:34,301
Shut up!

226
00:16:34,301 --> 00:16:35,301
I can't hear!

227
00:16:38,761 --> 00:16:39,581
Bring it on!

228
00:16:39,821 --> 00:16:41,161
We're not scared of you!

229
00:16:41,441 --> 00:16:42,321
Where's Saji?

230
00:16:42,401 --> 00:16:43,041
Wait, what?

231
00:16:43,141 --> 00:16:44,381
I don't know who that is.

232
00:16:44,941 --> 00:16:45,421
Saji!

233
00:16:45,761 --> 00:16:46,621
He's my friend!

234
00:16:46,861 --> 00:16:48,641
Sorry, never heard of him.

235
00:16:49,321 --> 00:16:50,121
Too bad.

236
00:16:50,741 --> 00:16:51,281
See ya!

237
00:16:55,021 --> 00:16:55,701
Shoot him!

238
00:16:55,701 --> 00:16:56,201
Hurry!

239
00:16:56,201 --> 00:16:57,201
Let's go!

240
00:16:59,021 --> 00:16:59,081
Get up!

241
00:16:59,081 --> 00:16:59,581
Get up!

242
00:17:00,021 --> 00:17:01,601
Straw Hat's coming out!

243
00:17:01,601 --> 00:17:06,961
Looks like they're shooting him, and he's saying no!

244
00:17:07,281 --> 00:17:10,261
Well, whatever happened, the train cars must be full of marines.

245
00:17:11,221 --> 00:17:13,361
So, what's the plan, rope man?

246
00:17:13,621 --> 00:17:16,681
If we don't move those cars out of the way, we might get knocked off!

247
00:21:55,340 --> 00:21:56,600
Guess I liked that one

248
00:21:57,600 --> 00:22:00,920
That's why there's one light

249
00:22:02,920 --> 00:22:05,340
I've been seen

250
00:22:06,760 --> 00:22:08,220
If I follow you

251
00:22:09,620 --> 00:22:12,740
All right, run away

252
00:22:13,400 --> 00:22:14,500
I won't be straight

253
00:22:17,080 --> 00:22:19,460
I've given you

254
00:22:20,080 --> 00:22:21,980
... always

255
00:22:22,520 --> 00:22:23,000
... attend

256
00:22:23,000 --> 00:22:51,640
Who the hell is that?

257
00:22:51,640 --> 00:22:53,880
Ah! That's the Ship Slasher!

258
00:22:53,880 --> 00:22:55,000
Ship Slasher?

259
00:22:55,000 --> 00:22:58,440
Ship Slasher T-Bone! A captain from Navy Headquarters!

260
00:22:58,440 --> 00:23:02,120
He uses a straight sword to cut through ships like a raw steak!

261
00:23:02,120 --> 00:23:03,160
Sounds like fun.

262
00:23:03,160 --> 00:23:06,200
Hey, Steak Man, draw your sword or get out of the way!

263
00:23:06,200 --> 00:23:08,680
On the next, One Piece, Clash!

264
00:23:08,680 --> 00:23:12,040
Demon Slasher Zorro vs. Ship Slasher T-Bone!

265
00:23:12,040 --> 00:23:13,960
I'm gonna be king of the pirates!

